# /usr/share/miadi/settings — the settings a Miadi host knows: a name, then
# what it does. `miadi-config settings` prints this file, and `miadi-config
# show` lists each of these even when unset. Replaced on upgrade: this host's
# values go in /etc/miadi/miadi.env, through `sudo miadi-config set`.

# Host layout
MIADI_ETC                        where miadi.env lives (default /etc/miadi)
MIADI_DATA_DIR                   the host's Miadi data (default /srv/miadi)
MIADI_WORK_DIR                   where repositories and wikis are cloned (default /workspace)
MIADI_REPOS_ROOT                 the cloned repositories (default $MIADI_WORK_DIR/repos)
MIADI_SRC                        the jgwill/Miadi checkout (default /src/Miadi)
MIADI_URL_BASE                   this host's public URL, the base of links that leave it (emailed invitations, QR codes); MIADI_WEBHOOK_URL and MIADI_PDE_WEBHOOK derive from it
MIADI_WEBHOOK_URL                where repository webhooks are pointed (default $MIADI_URL_BASE/api/workflow/webhook); set it on its own while webhooks still arrive through another front (gaia 2026-09-24: an ngrok URL, still hard-coded in binscripts fn_github.sh and bash_aliases_common instead of read from here)

# Read by miadi-terminal, on a client
MIADI_CHRONICLE_OPEN_URL         the Miadi front a clicked miadi-chronicle: reference opens on; unset, miadi-chronicle-open uses MIADI_URL_BASE

# Read by the Miadi app (jgwill/Miadi)
MIADI_API_URL                    the Miadi API the app and clients call (default http://127.0.0.1:3335)
MIADI_CHRONICLE_ROOT             the chronicle episodes (default $MIADI_EPISODES_DIR/miadi-chronicle)
MIADI_CHRONICLE_MW_URL           the chronicle medicine wheel (default http://127.0.0.1:8040)
MIADI_STORIES_ROOT               the Twine story library, a jgwill/miadi-passages checkout
MIADI_SESSIONDATA_ROOT           agent session capture (default /src/_sessiondata, else ~/_sessiondata)
MIADI_INQUIRY_ROOT               the inquiry artefact store the /v viewer admits
MIADI_IDENTITY_DIR               hashed person credentials (default $MIADI_DATA_DIR/identity)
MIADI_STUDIO_DIR                 the composition studio (default $MIADI_EPISODES_DIR/miadi-studio)
MIADI_VIEW_ROOTS                 colon-separated absolute paths the /v viewer serves; replaces config/view-roots.json
MIADI_HOST_TYPE                  local or cloud (the app treats unset as local)
MIADI_MIACO_BIN                  absolute path of the miaco binary, for the PDE milestone chain
MIADI_PDE_STEER_TIMEOUT_MS       PDE steer timeout in milliseconds (the app's default is 900000)
MIADI_GATE_TRUST_LOOPBACK_HOST   1 only when the server binds 127.0.0.1; off when unset
MIADI_TRUST_TAILNET_SERVICE      hostname of the Tailscale Service that fronts the app; off when unset
MIADI_TAILNET_LOGINS             comma-separated Tailscale logins granted reader and writer over that service
MIADI_FLOWISE_ENABLED            1 re-enables the Flowise proxy; off when unset
MIADI_STEER_DEV_BYPASS           1 lets /api/tide/steer run without a writer token outside production; off when unset
MIADI_MAIL_FROM                  the sender of the mail Miadi sends, e.g. Miadi <miadi@your-domain>; with MIADI_SMTP_URL unset, no mail leaves
MIADI_SMTP_URL                   secret, the SMTP relay with its credential (smtps://user:password@host:465); kept in the service's env file, never in miadi.env
MIADI_API_TOKEN_WRITER           secret, read and write; kept in ~/.env or the service's env file, never in miadi.env
MIADI_API_TOKEN_READER           secret, read only; kept in ~/.env or the service's env file, never in miadi.env
